{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1329,
    "dDurationMs": 4161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This video is based on joke presentation I\ngave last year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5490,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was recently on the phone with an internet\nservice provider whose name shall remain unspoken"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 9690,
    "dDurationMs": 4239,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they promised me their mediocre internet\nservices for one price and then charged me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 13929,
    "dDurationMs": 4891,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "another price . And you may not be surprised\nto hear that price B was greater than price"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18820,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A. So I was on the phone to see if I could\nget B to equal to A."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22990,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which reminds me of the first of the axioms\nof Zermelo-Fraenkel set theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28470,
    "dDurationMs": 5750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For those of you who don’t know, Zermelo-Fraenkel\nset theory is the, how shall I put it – pedantry?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34220,
    "dDurationMs": 2729,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that forms the foundation of modern mathematics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 36949,
    "dDurationMs": 2671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And to get a good idea, you only really need\nto know two things about it:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 39620,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– it exists (that’s a math joke, though\nI guess so is this whole talk)"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43790,
    "dDurationMs": 5170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "– and, using the Zermelo-Fraenkel axioms,\nthe number 2 is written like this , which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48960,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in English reads “the set that contains\nthe set that contains only the set containing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53360,
    "dDurationMs": 2380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "nothing as well as the set containing nothing”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55740,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can see the logicians in the audience are\nloving this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58220,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, so the first axiom of Zermelo-Fraenkel\nset theory says that two sets are equal if"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 63610,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they have the same elements."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64890,
    "dDurationMs": 4210,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, the internet company that shall not\nbe named was providing the same set of services"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69100,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for different prices – . So B≠A, but they\nboth contain the same set of services… this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75220,
    "dDurationMs": 3850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a violation the first axiom of Zermelo-Fraenkel\nset theory."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79070,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At this point, perhaps, I should have been\nworried."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81470,
    "dDurationMs": 1450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But I continued nevertheless."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82920,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I again asked for price A."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 85430,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they replied: “The option we offered\nIS all that we can offer.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 90070,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I was horrified."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91070,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For, you see, the second axiom of Zermelo-Fraenkel\nset theory implies that a set cannot be a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95590,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "member of itself, and yet they had just said\nthat the set of all options they could offer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99830,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was the same as the option they offered, which\nclearly must be contained in the set of all"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104150,
    "dDurationMs": 1690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "options they could offer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105840,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And thus they violated the second axiom upon\nwhich modern mathematics is built."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109990,
    "dDurationMs": 4131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“Let me speak to your manager” I said,\nwhich is code for “I think your working"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 114121,
    "dDurationMs": 1089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "axiomatic system is crap.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115210,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, as expected, the manager did not immediately\nimprove the situation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119250,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just so we’re all on the same page, I simply\nwanted internet for the promised price A,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123750,
    "dDurationMs": 5679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "let’s say, $40, but had been charged B,\nsay, $50 for the same service."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129429,
    "dDurationMs": 2831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And I had been told that “$50 is the best\noffer they can make.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132260,
    "dDurationMs": 5890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The manager promptly offered me internet,\nPLUS a home wifi router, for $45."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138150,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You might think this is an improvement, as\ndid I until I asked if I could have the offer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142390,
    "dDurationMs": 4830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of internet plus router, but hold the router,\nand I was told “No.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147220,
    "dDurationMs": 3890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The third axiom of Zermelo-Fraenkel set theory\nwas not happy with that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151110,
    "dDurationMs": 3190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because you’re supposed to be able to make\na subset out of elements of a set, and have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 154300,
    "dDurationMs": 4340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that also be a set, but apparently not in\nthe world of ISPs."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158640,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This also violates axiom 6 , by the way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161920,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fifth axiom , combining existing sets\ntogether into new sets – well, I have to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166040,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "give it to the internet companies; they’ve\ngot this down pat: they call it “bundling”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169620,
    "dDurationMs": 5410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The violation of the seventh Axiom, the axiom\nof infinity, is, to be honest, more a criticism"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175030,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of modern mathematics than telecommunication\ncompanies (though they still violate it)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179260,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Speaking as a physicist, I can tell you that\ninternet service providers and any other physical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183180,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thing in our apparently non-continuous, finite-sized\nobservable universe – they can’t have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187580,
    "dDurationMs": 1860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "an infinite amount of anything."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 189440,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I can’t even say they have an infinite absence\nof customer service, because that would require"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193180,
    "dDurationMs": 3309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the possibility of an infinite amount for\nthem to be lacking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196489,
    "dDurationMs": 4871,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But there was still something bugging me – the\nmanager told me that the offer for $45 was"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201360,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "comprised of internet for $40 a month, plus\n5 bucks a month for the router."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205810,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So breaking things down: the possible monthly\nservices provided include {internet for $40,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210620,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "internet for $50, TV, phone, and wifi router\nfor $5}."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214770,
    "dDurationMs": 4730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, it was clear that “internet for $40”\nwas an element of the set called “internet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 219500,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "plus router”, and “internet plus router”\nwas an element of “possible service combinations”,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224500,
    "dDurationMs": 3379,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "while “internet for $40”, on its own,\nwas not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227879,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet, the possible service combinations\nshould include all possible combinations of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232319,
    "dDurationMs": 3661,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "services, which Zermelo-Fraenkel would call\nthe power set."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 235980,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And thus I realized that the 8th axiom was\nviolated (and, also, the 4th)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240440,
    "dDurationMs": 5519,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I think at this point we’d hit all 8 axioms,\nand my internet company violated 7 out of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245959,
    "dDurationMs": 4201,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "8 – but as all of you doubtless know, the\nstandard Zermelo-Fraenkel axioms often come"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250160,
    "dDurationMs": 2159,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "packaged with a 9th axiom."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 252319,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you need only see the name to know this\naxiom is seriously violated by telecommunications"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 258319,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "companies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259319,
    "dDurationMs": 4921,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so, I almost despaired, except despair\ncan’t be constructed without the Axiom schema"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264240,
    "dDurationMs": 1419,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of specification ."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 265659,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And then I remembered something important:\neven if all of the axioms I hold dear are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270979,
    "dDurationMs": 3090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "violated, that doesn’t mean there’s no\nlogic or reason remaining."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274069,
    "dDurationMs": 5250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What’s “true” in the mathematical world\ndepends on what underlying axioms you take"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 279319,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be true."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280319,
    "dDurationMs": 2581,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I said “Hang on,” and took a deep breath."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282900,
    "dDurationMs": 6289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "“Can I get the 45 dollar option, which consists\nof internet for $40 and a router for 5 bucks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289189,
    "dDurationMs": 2961,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a month, and then just send you back the router\nso I don’t have to pay for it?”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292150,
    "dDurationMs": 2319,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you know what the guy from the internet\ncompany told me?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294469,
    "dDurationMs": 5061,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "He told me what every scheming mathematician\nwants to hear from their axioms: “I can’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299530,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tell you you can’t do that.”"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302610,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The End"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304930,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This story is partly based on the truth (I’ll\nleave you to figure out which parts), and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 308950,
    "dDurationMs": 4189,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I first told it at the festival of Bad Ad-Hoc\nHypotheses (BAHFest), where the idea is to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313139,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "listen to crazy made up scientific theories\nin the hope that we’ll be, well, both entertained,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317639,
    "dDurationMs": 2550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more aware of how science actually works."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 320189,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can listen to more entertaining stories\n(science and otherwise) on Audible, this video’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 325249,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sponsor."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326249,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Audible has the largest selection of audiobooks\non the planet, including best-sellers, mysteries,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330129,
    "dDurationMs": 6091,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "memoirs, originals, and science books - I\nvery much enjoyed “How Not To Be Wrong”,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336220,
    "dDurationMs": 5610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by Jordan Ellenberg, a more correct but similarly\nsarcastic book about how to use simple math"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341830,
    "dDurationMs": 4329,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to not be wrong (it has plenty of fascinating\nstories of big mistakes that have been made"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346159,
    "dDurationMs": 3870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because people misused math)."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 350029,
    "dDurationMs": 5271,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To start listening with a 30-day trial, go\nto audible.com/minutephysics or text ‘minutephysics’"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355300,
    "dDurationMs": 4989,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to 500500 and you can choose 1 audiobook and\n2 audible originals each month."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360289,
    "dDurationMs": 5362,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Again, that’s audible.com/minutephysics\nor text ‘minutephysics’ to 500500, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 365651,
    "dDurationMs": 1528,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thanks to Audible for supporting MinutePhysics."
    } ]
  } ]
}
